     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">I´m wondering if the zmax value can be changed in plot.rf. I have LOD values around 30 for small recombination fractions in my pairwise data.<br>I´m using  zmax=30, this can be done?</blockquote><div><br></div><div><span style=\"line-height:18px\">You can specify zmax in the call to plot.rf. Here&#39;s an example:</span></div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    library(qtl)</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">   </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\"> </span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">data(fake.f2)</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">   </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\"> </span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">fake.f2 &lt;- est.rf(fake.f2)</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">   </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\"> </span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">plot.rf(fake.f2, zmax=5)</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">   </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\"> </span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">plot.rf(fake.f2, zmax=6) </font></div><div><br></div><div>karl</div></div>"
